within a <span class=\"strong\">sentence</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Most sentences have two basic types of words:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Content Words</span> <br><ul><li>Content words are the important or key words in a sentence. They provide the meaning of the sentence</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Structure Words</span> <br><ul><li>Structure words are not important words. They are small words that you use to make the sentence correct. </li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:<span class=\"italic\"> <span class=\"strong\">I</span> do <span class=\"strong\">not want</span> to <span class=\"strong\">stay</span>.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The content words are in bold.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Stressing New Information</span><br>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You pronounce information that is new with stress, since it is more important to the listener. <br/>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example: <br/><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Sara</span>: Where do you come from? <br/><span class=\"strong\">Sonya</span>: I'm from <span class=\"strong\">London</span>.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The fact that Sonya is from London is new to Sara, thus it is stressed.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "energy", "type": "name"}, {"content": "ability to be active ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Your child has a lot of energy.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le05ob04aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you hear in a conversation at a restaurant.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to stomp ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to step on very forcefully ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}